      "writtenOn": "2021-01-08T22:48:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will that actually work?  If the screen refresh isn\u0027t exactly 60 Hz (and usually it isn\u0027t) or if clock division means that we can\u0027t actually make exactly 1400 Hz then maybe it\u0027d actually be worse to try to be divisible by 60 Hz?  I could imagine some bad \"beat\" patterns if you have two rates that are close but not exact and things might actually be better if they were totally not divisible?\n\n...but also: does this matter?  I know for refresh rate and lighting frequency it matters, but for PWM backlight isn\u0027t there smoothing in the system (maybe the natural decay of the LED output?) that means you can\u0027t actually observe this frequency?\n\n(if the above makes no sense, please ignore--I may have a bad understanding of how all this works).",
